me=\"new-file\">Create absent files/directories in order; parents must exist or be created earlier. No inspect/read or overwrite. Per-entry errors preserve successes; retry only failures.</tool>\n    <tool name=\"delete-file\">Delete a nonempty list of workroot-relative paths; directories are recursive. Reject the workroot and directly named symlinks; never follow nested symlinks. No inspect/read required. Ordered per-path results; failures keep earlier effects.</tool>\n  </sub-tools>\n  <parameter-descriptions path-format=\"json-pointer\">\n    <tool name=\"edit-file\">\n      <parameter path=\"/properties/edits\" type=\"string\">One string: &lt;exmekh_edit path=\"file.txt\" id=\"123\" /&gt;old text&lt;exmekh_new_text id=\"123\"/&gt;new text. The server supplies the opening ID; copy it into the separator; omit IDs only for unambiguous framing. Bodies are exact literal text: preserve whitespace/newlines; no entity or CDATA decoding. Append edits with fresh IDs; new text ends at the next opening or string end. Empty new text removes the selection, not the file. Insert by retaining an anchor in new text. Empty old text requires an existing empty file. No command tags.</parameter>\n    </tool>\n    <tool name=\"new-file\">\n      <parameter path=\"/properties/document\" type=\"string\">&lt;new-exmekh-dir path=\"folder\"/&gt;&lt;new-exmekh-file path=\"folder/file.txt\"/&gt;content. Self-closing markers have only a double-quoted path, entity-decoded. Each body ends at the next reserved new-exmekh-file/new-exmekh-dir opening prefix or string end; no closing tags or escaping those prefixes. File bodies need &gt;=2 Unicode characters, preserved literally without trimming, entity decoding or added newlines. Directory bodies are ignored with warnings.</parameter>\n    </tool>\n  </parameter-descriptions>\n</catalog>\n\n<exit-tool name=\"exit_agent\">Call exit_agent to close only this skill. Its inner transcript leaves active context:\n`text` must preserve the outcome, completed actions, essential facts/references and next step.\nPromote full outputs in `items` only when the caller needs their details now; otherwise use `items=[]`.\nFor use inside a later skill, put the ID/path and purpose in `text` and retrieve there.\n\n`items` accepts saved outputs only from this invocation or descendants. Prefer canonical\n`saved-output-id`; an unambiguous call ID is accepted. No duplicate aliases or unsaved memory reads.\n\n\nPlace with `{{output-id}}` and list that output in `items` (either alias may identify the same record).\nUnplaced items append in list order as `&lt;tool-output&gt;` XML; large outputs stay file manifests.\n\nAn exit error keeps the skill open: correct the arguments and retry the exit, not the completed work.</exit-tool>"}],"stream":true,"reasoning":{"effort":"none"},"tool_choice":"required","tools":[{"type":"function","name":"file-processing","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"strict":true,"description":"Open a scope for workspace files. Inspect. Read. Edit. Create. Delete."},{"type":"function","name":"delete-file","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"additionalProperties":false,"required":["paths"]},"strict":true,"description":"Requires open skill 'file-processing'."},{"type":"function","name":"edit-file","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"edits":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false,"required":["edits"]},"strict":true,"description":"Requires open skill 'file-processing'."},{"type":"function","name":"inspect-file","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"detailed":{"type":"boolean"},"max_items":{"type":"integer"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"query":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"execution_mode":{"anyOf":[{"enum":["wait","background"],"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"wait_seconds":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false,"req